{
  "review_date": "2026-11-27",
  "upstream_commit": "868d022adfdc3740449241f4721debbf4b1b1426",
  "scope": "All 24 vendored upstream files plus cspenguin.nix and nixos.patch. Text reviewed; 11 executables inspected statically for file type, imports and printable strings. PNG and font identified and hashed only. No execution, antivirus scan, full disassembly or binary/source equivalence verification. Runtime downloads excluded.",
  "conclusion": "No explicit credential theft, exfiltration or hidden remote control found in reviewed text. Binary safety is unverified.",
  "findings": [
    "11 prebuilt executables are installed without verifying equivalence to source.",
    "Media Foundation patch fails git apply --numstat: corrupt patch at line 30; source-to-binary reproduction is not established.",
    "Winetricks master and missing assets from main are mutable; most runtime downloads lack checksum verification (Gecko is an exception).",
    "WebView2 is launched with --no-sandbox. FHS environment is not a security boundary for home files.",
    "Thumbnailer uses predictable /tmp/clip-thumbnailer-PID.db with File::create; possible symlink/clobber hazard subject to OS protections, and failure paths leave artwork data behind.",
    "Uninstall recursively deletes supplied WINEPREFIX without guarding dangerous values; install deletes matching CSP desktop entries across prefixes.",
    "Prewarm systemd user service is prompted with default yes, not hidden persistence.",
    "NixOS patch removes limits.d/user manager limit writes, but does not eliminate the other upstream risks."
  ],
